-sname ${HB_ERL_SNAME:-"hb"}
## Idle schedulers sleep instead of spinning: on a shared box the spin
## burned several cores that request and Lua work needed (PARALITH.md).
+sbwt none
+sbwtdcpu none
+sbwtdio none
## Dirty CPU schedulers run wasm-patch@1.0 slots (hb_wasm_nif): AOT code
## and its natives use the native stack, so give them 2048 kilowords (16 MB).
+sssdcpu 2048
## Dirty IO threads: every LMDB scan, synced commit and env sync is a
## DirtyIo NIF, and a synced commit holds its thread through an fsync (and
## the env's one write lock). With the default 10, fifteen busy processes
## queued scans behind commits: lmdb_scan 4.5 ms mean. 64: 2.3-3.6 ms,
## +37% node-wide msg/s, -12% CPU per message (bench/msgpath.mjs, 15 procs).
+SDio 64
